From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Heinemeier Hansson <david@hey.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 07:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: qcom: declare the Zenbook A16 router image

The router driver requests its firmware once, at probe, which happens in
the initramfs once mkinitcpio has picked up thunderbolt_qcom. mkinitcpio
only copies firmware a module declares, so the image the ASUS Zenbook A16
(UX3607OA) device tree names must be declared as well, or the router
probe fails in the initramfs for want of a file that is on the root
filesystem.

The image is the same one the Surface Laptop 8 uses (SHA-256 0f2eb991...):
ASUS's Qualcomm board support package for the UX3607OA carries the same
QcUsb4Filter8480.sys router image. It is kept under the board's own
firmware directory, next to its DSP images.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
---
 drivers/thunderbolt/qcom-usb4-host.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/qcom-usb4-host.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/qcom-usb4-host.c
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/qcom-usb4-host.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/qcom-usb4-host.c
@@ -1700,8 +1700,9 @@
 	{ }
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, qcom_usb4_host_of_match);
-/* Router image named by the Surface Laptop 8 device tree, for initramfs tools. */
+/* Router images named by the board device trees, for initramfs tools. */
 MODULE_FIRMWARE("qcom/glymur/surface-laptop8/usb4-router-legacy.bin");
+MODULE_FIRMWARE("qcom/glymur/ASUSTeK/UX3607OA/usb4-router-legacy.bin");
 
 static struct platform_driver qcom_usb4_host_driver = {
 	.probe = qcom_usb4_host_probe,
